  "title": "ErrorBoundary Go Home button navigates to /retailer/ but ProtectedRoute expects /s/:storeCode path",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: Navigation. Severity: P2. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The ErrorBoundary's 'Go to Home' button (line 35) navigates to '/retailer/' using window.location.href. However, the app's routing structure expects authenticated users to be at `/s/:storeCode/` paths. Navigating to '/retailer/' would hit the root route which redirects based on auth state. If the user is authenticated, they'll be redirected to their store dashboard, but this is an unnecessary round trip. If the auth state is corrupted (which is possible since we're in an error boundary), the user may end up in a redirect loop.",
